==Danish==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|da|fr|parti}}, {{m|fr|partie}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|da|/parti/|[pʰaˈtˢiːˀ]}}

===Noun===
{{da-noun|et|er}}

# [[lot]], [[quantity]], [[batch]]
#: {{ux|da|Vi har købt et '''parti''' hvidløg.|We have bought a '''batch''' of garlic.}}
#* {{quote-book|da|year=1873|author=Norway. Departementet for det indre|title=Uddrag af consulatberetninger vedkommende Norges handel og skibsfart|page=67
|passage=Fra Island, Skotland etc. er intet '''Parti''' Fisk ankommet til dette Distrikt.
|translation=From Iceland, Scotland etc., no '''batch''' of fish has arrived to this district.}}
# {{lb|da|politics}} [[political party|party]]
# [[game]] (of e.g. chess or tennis)
#: {{ux|da|Skal vi tage et '''parti''' skak?|Shall we play a '''game''' of chess?}}
# A prospective spouse perceived as an economical or social boon rather than a person; a {{l|en|parti}}
#: {{ux|da|Han ansås som det bedste '''parti''' på øen.|He was seen as the best '''parti''' on the island.}}
#* {{quote-book|da|year=2007|author=Rushy Rashid|title=Et løft af sløret|publisher=Art People|isbn=9788771374261
|passage=Vennen havde en nevø, som skulle være et godt '''parti''' - og som ville acceptere, at jeg havde været gift tidligere.
|t=The friend had a nephew, who was allegedly a good '''parti''' - and who would accept that I had been married before.}}
#* {{quote-book|da|year=2016|author=John Nehm|title=Dagen og vejen|publisher=Lindhardt og Ringhof|isbn=9788711491171
|passage=Han var et godt '''parti'''. Et godt '''parti'''! Hun sukkede. Herman havde giftet sig med Lydia fordi han troede, at han elskede hende.
|t=He was a good '''parti'''. A good '''parti'''! She sighed. Herman had married Lydia because he thought he loved her.}}
#* {{quote-book|da|year=2010|author=Michael Bregnsbo|title=Til venstre hånd: danske kongers elskerinder|publisher=Gyldendal A/S|isbn=9788702065749|page=76
|passage=At hun kunne gøre et så godt '''parti''', tyder på, at adelen modsat kongen ikke var så forarget over hendes affære med prins Christian, selv om man selvfølgelig heller ikke bør se bort fra, at hun med sit særdeles omfattende jordegods nu en gang var et godt '''parti'''.
|t=That she could get so good a '''husband''' would indicate that the nobility, as opposed to the king, was not so offended by her affair with prince Christian, although, naturally, one must keep in mind that, with her quite expansive properties of land, she was after all a good '''parti'''.}}
# [[part]]
# [[side]]

